        "t0": {
          "issueOrPullRequest": {
            "__typename": "PullRequest",
            "id": "PR_kwDOErHI988AAAABMCorRw",
            "number": 1625,
            "title": "fix: return 412 for matching If-None-Match on non-GET/HEAD in handleCacheHeaders",
            "body": "`handleCacheHeaders` returned `304 Not Modified` for every method when the cache validators matched. Per RFC 9110:\n\n- §13.1.2: a matching `If-None-Match` on a method other than GET/HEAD must fail the request with `412 Precondition Failed`, not `304`;\n- §13.2.1: conditional headers must be ignored for OPTIONS, TRACE and CONNECT;\n- §13.1.3: `If-Modified-Since` must be ignored for methods other than GET/HEAD.\n\nThe fix keeps the helper's control-flow contract (returns `true` = stop) while selecting the right status: 304 for GET/HEAD, 412 for a matching `If-None-Match` on other methods, and `false` (handler runs normally) for the ignore cases. Added four tests covering POST/PUT → 412, HEAD → 304, POST + If-Modified-Since-only → 200, and OPTIONS → 200.\n\nFixes #1623.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Corrected conditional cache responses: matching ETags now return the appropriate status for GET, HEAD, and other methods.\n  * OPTIONS, TRACE, and CONNECT requests now proceed without conditional cache headers affecting their response.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
