        "t1": {
          "issueOrPullRequest": {
            "__typename": "PullRequest",
            "id": "PR_kwDOErHI988AAAABL63ZEg",
            "number": 1624,
            "title": "fix(cache): honor request methods when evaluating cache headers",
            "body": "resolves #1623\n\nMatching `If-None-Match` preconditions stop POST, PUT, PATCH, and DELETE with `412` rather than `304` ([RFC 9110 §13.1.2](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110#section-13.1.2)). These methods ignore `If-Modified-Since`; OPTIONS, TRACE, and CONNECT ignore conditional headers ([§13.2.1](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110#section-13.2.1)). GET, HEAD, and QUERY retain their existing `304` behavior.\n\nThe issue includes a runnable reproduction. Regression tests cover both web and Node adapters, including weak tags, wildcards, nonmatches, and validator overrides; helper-level tests also cover TRACE and CONNECT. They fail with only the source changes reverted.\n\n`pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm build`, and the affected suites passed. Local `pnpm test`: 3,219 passed, 51 skipped, one Node body-limit timeout; unchanged main at f0e1780: 3,128 passed, 51 skipped, two body-limit timeouts, including the same test.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Conditional cache validation now returns `304 Not Modified` for matching validators on `GET`, `HEAD`, and `QUERY` requests.\n  * For other methods, a matching `If-None-Match` returns `412 Precondition Failed`; `If-Modified-Since` does not trigger a conditional response.\n  * `CONNECT`, `OPTIONS`, and `TRACE` requests ignore both conditional headers and continue processing.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Clarified how conditional cache headers are handled across request methods.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
