        "t2": {
          "issueOrPullRequest": {
            "__typename": "PullRequest",
            "id": "PR_kwDOErHI988AAAABLiBkhA",
            "number": 1622,
            "title": "fix: keep `Server-Timing` entries on error responses and when merging headers",
            "body": "Error responses (thrown errors, 404s, returned responses with status >= 400) only receive headers staged on `event.res.errHeaders`. `setServerTiming()` only wrote to `event.res.headers`, so its entries were dropped from error responses,\n\n- `setServerTiming()` now also writes to `event.res.errHeaders`, like the CORS utils do.\n- `mergeHeaders()` now keeps both sides of `Server-Timing` (staged entries first, then the response's own) instead of replacing them. Without this, the change above would wipe a returned error response's own entries.\n\n```ts\napp.use((event) => setServerTiming(event, \"auth\", { dur: 1 }));\napp.get(\"/fail\", () => {\n  throw new HTTPError({ status: 503, headers: { \"server-timing\": \"upstream;dur=9\" } });\n});\n// before: server-timing: upstream;dur=9\n// after:  server-timing: auth;dur=1, upstream;dur=9\n```\n\nUsed for nitrojs/nitro#4904\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Server timing information is now retained on error responses, including when a handler or measured operation fails.\n  * Timing entries from middleware and handlers are combined without duplicating entries on cached responses.\n  * When multiple `Server-Timing` values are combined, staged entries appear before existing values. Other response-header behavior remains unchanged.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
